;;; `open` written as a conclusion's argument loads, and a rule derives a fact
;;; about it — regression `conclusion-value`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `r` concludes `(p open)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `open` is a name wherever the kernel does not read it, at the head of a
;;; written fact, a premise or a conclusion, and under an ordinary relation the
;;; head of a fact the kernel does not read (Q-M1f.66, Q-M1f.571): here it is
;;; written as a conclusion's argument, so the program loads, and every command
;;; answers.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `f62e34e1`, release: the program loads, root derives `(p open)`, and R is
;;; 16 states, exit 0 on every command.
;;; The engine loads it.
;;;

(relation a Thing :why "{?3} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?3} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?3} is a q")
(is-a k Thing)
(a k)
(rule r ()
  :match  (a ?x)
  :assert (p open)
  :why "{?x} is an a, so open is a p")
